        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[[xhr] FormData and its iterable methods (keys, entries, values) should mention possibility of duplicate keys]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45582</link>
            <guid>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45582</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 21:19:59 GMT</pubDate>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p dir="auto">A <code class="notranslate">&lt;form&gt;</code> and <code class="notranslate">FormData</code> is often viewed as a key-value map, including methods common to iterable objects:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/entries" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/entries</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/keys" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/keys</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/values" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/values</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Unlike iterable objects such as <code class="notranslate">Map</code>, <code class="notranslate">FormData</code> can have multiple key-value pairs with the same key (this follows from the fact that a <code class="notranslate">&lt;form&gt;</code> can have multiple elements with the same name). A naive iteration over a <code class="notranslate">FormData</code> with the assumption of the keys being unique can result in bugs. So it would be helpful if these methods explicitly call out that keys are not necessarily unique; and that the <code class="notranslate">get</code> or <code class="notranslate">getAll</code> method of <code class="notranslate">FormData</code> should be used depending on the intended use case.</p>
<p dir="auto">The top-level documentation does not make it obvious either: <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/FormData" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FormData/FormData</a></p>
<p dir="auto">If you want to verify manually, here is an example:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="&lt;form id=&quot;dupeform&quot;&gt;
 &lt;input name=&quot;dupekey&quot; value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
 &lt;input name=&quot;dupekey&quot; value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
let fd = new FormData(document.getElementById(&quot;dupeform&quot;));
console.log(Array.from(fd.keys())); // [&quot;dupekey&quot;, &quot;dupekey&quot;]
console.log(Array.from(fd.entries())); // [[&quot;dupekey&quot;, &quot;1&quot;], [&quot;dupekey&quot;, &quot;2&quot;]]
console.log(Array.from(fd.values())); // [&quot;1&quot;, &quot;2&quot;]

// Example of potential bug: lost a value
console.log(new Map(fd)); // Map with one entry, &quot;dupekey&quot; with value &quot;2&quot;; lost&quot;1&quot;.
&lt;/script&gt;"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class="pl-ent">form</span> <span class="pl-c1">id</span>="<span class="pl-s">dupeform</span>"<span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
 <span class="pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class="pl-ent">input</span> <span class="pl-c1">name</span>="<span class="pl-s">dupekey</span>" <span class="pl-c1">value</span>="<span class="pl-s">1</span>"<span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
 <span class="pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class="pl-ent">input</span> <span class="pl-c1">name</span>="<span class="pl-s">dupekey</span>" <span class="pl-c1">value</span>="<span class="pl-s">2</span>"<span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
<span class="pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class="pl-ent">form</span><span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
<span class="pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class="pl-ent">script</span><span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
<span class="pl-k">let</span> <span class="pl-s1">fd</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-k">new</span> <span class="pl-v">FormData</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-smi">document</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">getElementById</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">"dupeform"</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-v">Array</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">from</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">fd</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">keys</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span> <span class="pl-c">// ["dupekey", "dupekey"]</span>
<span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-v">Array</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">from</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">fd</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">entries</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span> <span class="pl-c">// [["dupekey", "1"], ["dupekey", "2"]]</span>
<span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-v">Array</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">from</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">fd</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">values</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span> <span class="pl-c">// ["1", "2"]</span>

<span class="pl-c">// Example of potential bug: lost a value</span>
<span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-k">new</span> <span class="pl-v">Map</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">fd</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span> <span class="pl-c">// Map with one entry, "dupekey" with value "2"; lost"1".</span>
<span class="pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class="pl-ent">script</span><span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">This behavior is not new, the wpt test verifying the behavior across browsers was checked in 10 years ago: <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/f8fa38984dbd1527b2fa292b2527c39c1605ba27/hovercard" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/f8fa38984dbd1527b2fa292b2527c39c1605ba27">web-platform-tests/wpt@<tt>f8fa389</tt></a> (test has moved since then, but is still here: <a href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blame/7926f3ca1cd9f7f1df88db0bb0cee14f278a559b/xhr/formdata/foreach.any.js">https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blame/7926f3ca1cd9f7f1df88db0bb0cee14f278a559b/xhr/formdata/foreach.any.js</a> )</p>]]></content:encoded>
